395 0 obj
<<
/Title (The power system is divided into two branches: a high-current motor rail and a regulated electronics rail. The motor rail powers the drive motors through the Carobot V3 motor shield, while the dispensing stepper motor is supplied via a 5V buck converter. The OpenMV cameras are powered from a dedicated regulated supply to prevent voltage transients from causing camera resets. The regulated logic rail supplies the distance sensors, IMU, and colour sensor. The Arduino GIGA R1 operates on 3.3V logic, so all high-current devices are driven through dedicated driver electronics rather than directly from GPIO pins.)
/Dest [9 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 13 0 R
/Prev 720 0 R
/First 721 0 R
/Last 722 0 R
/Count -6
/Next 161 0 R
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Title (The robot uses a state machine as its core software architecture, navigating tile by tile through the maze. The maze is mapped using a 2D array of custom tile bitsets, storing wall data, victim records, and exploration states. Breadth-first search calculates the return path to the starting tile. The Arduino GIGA's dual-core processor divides responsibilities: the M7 core handles navigation, PID motor control, mapping, and BFS, while the M4 core continuously monitors the OpenMV cameras for victim detections.)
/Dest [9 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 161 0 R
/First 723 0 R
/Last 723 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
